#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091933 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "5d895685-fc8e-57ca-9552-1d3d2e0202a0" :question/math-academy-id "e-3513" :question/problem "Calculate, in degrees to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation $\\tan x=4$ for $0 \\leq x < 360^\\circ$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan (4) = 75.96375...^{∘} \\approx 75.964^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $75.964^\\circ$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is\n\n$$\nx_1 = 75.964^\\circ\n$$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $180^\\circ$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx_2 = 180^\\circ + 75.964^\\circ \\approx 255.964^\\circ\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions (rounded to the nearest integer) are\n\n$$\nx=76^\\circ, 256^\\circ\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091934 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Special Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "8efb6790-c3c0-5639-bb5d-61b774e1fa60" :question/math-academy-id "e-3514" :question/problem "Find the solutions to the equation $3\\tan x + 3\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $0^\\circ \\leq x < 360^\\circ$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\tan x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\tan x + 3\\sqrt{3} &= 0 \\\\\n3\\tan x &= -3\\sqrt{3} \\\\\n\\tan x &= -\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\\n\\tan x &= -\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan (-\\sqrt{3}) =-60^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $-60^\\circ$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution. However, to generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $180^\\circ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= x + 180^{∘} =-60^{∘} + 180^{∘} = 120^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{2} &= x + 360^{∘} =-60^{∘} + 360^{∘} = 300^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=120^\\circ, 300^\\circ\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091935 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/id #uuid "d50d2e80-594a-5512-8ebb-f82082def313" :question/math-academy-id "e-3515" :question/problem "Solve the equation $3 \\tan x - \\sqrt{3} = 0$ for $-180^\\circ < x \\leq 180^\\circ$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\tan x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\tan x - \\sqrt{3} &= 0 \\\\\n3\\tan x &= \\sqrt{3} \\\\\n\\tan x &= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) = 30^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $30^\\circ$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is\n\n$$\nx_1 =30^\\circ\n$$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we subtract integer multiples of $180^\\circ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{2} &= x_{1} - 180^{∘} \\\\\n&= 30^{∘} - 180^{∘} \\\\\n&=-150^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=-150^\\circ, 30^\\circ\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091936 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "3311aab4-1938-543c-a84c-d285a905dada" :question/math-academy-id "e-3516" :question/problem "The graph below shows a section of the curve $y=\\tan{x}$ on the interval $-\\dfrac \\pi 2 < x < \\dfrac {\\pi} 2$ and the line $y=1$. The line and the curve intersect at the point $A$, as shown. What is the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/915/Source/Images/75d3912698b1187b3fc86e2e9db62892.png)" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two functions gives\n\n$$\n\\tan x=1, \\qquad -\\dfrac \\pi 2 < x < \\dfrac {\\pi} 2\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan (1) = \\frac{π}{4}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nlies inside the required domain, and there is only one point of intersection, we conclude that the $x$-coordinate of the intersection point $A$ is\n\n$$\nx= \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9a1e997-df29-5cf1-951f-f9868235631f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265678} {:answer/id #uuid "0e7952ae-af35-5750-a059-6b2e161687a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265679} {:answer/id #uuid "ce09e2d0-9123-5abb-85b7-c28d592a180d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265680} {:answer/id #uuid "f849dc82-cff0-5379-98d0-5d57e99be843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265681} {:answer/id #uuid "94b3a771-ad77-555f-8969-4c9ee99117c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9a1e997-df29-5cf1-951f-f9868235631f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265678} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecb8e0f4-e168-500b-bf2b-e5e2dcb5f9aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265677}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b26e4756-90f6-541a-8bf3-78caf4240c2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-121119" :question/problem "Solve the equation $7\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2\\sqrt{3}=-5\\sqrt{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2\\sqrt{3} & =-5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-7\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=\\pi +(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=2\\pi +(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e024257-6d61-51eb-b36f-10514fa1c377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={85}^{∘},{265}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265685} {:answer/id #uuid "1a3a3a81-ab91-5a37-81bc-40fe8fcf4d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={69}^{∘},{249}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265686} {:answer/id #uuid "3e863113-e050-5e61-8a8c-85b2d57826af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={65}^{∘},{245}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265687} {:answer/id #uuid "279b1ee2-1cde-5701-a219-5c59a7d40a99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={91}^{∘},{271}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265688} {:answer/id #uuid "8320ce09-598c-5036-a8e1-120f1822df01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={72}^{∘},{252}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e024257-6d61-51eb-b36f-10514fa1c377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={85}^{∘},{265}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265685} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8bdec1e-5039-50b4-9d7c-35a12b29d275" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265684}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e51ee52-43c9-52c5-87d3-c93144f63c70" :question/math-academy-id "q-121130" :question/problem "Solve the equation $3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-33=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ rounded to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-33=0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =33 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext,  we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(11)=84.805\\,571{…}^{∘}≈{84.81}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${84.81}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={84.81}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{84.81}^{∘}={264.81}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx={85}^{∘},{265}^{∘}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf29bd25-be25-5596-a87c-7bca5ce573fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={93}^{∘},{273}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265692} {:answer/id #uuid "85557900-af23-574e-85ae-7ab0032c6bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={80}^{∘},{260}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265693} {:answer/id #uuid "9144e89e-5100-5e9d-8661-2edd52be6f10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={71}^{∘},{251}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265694} {:answer/id #uuid "973efc20-dfb3-520d-9663-e910b0c8d731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={86}^{∘},{266}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265695} {:answer/id #uuid "9f93e05f-9fac-5ad6-ad61-3991aeed37b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={74}^{∘},{254}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "973efc20-dfb3-520d-9663-e910b0c8d731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={86}^{∘},{266}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265695} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d0979c4-a6bf-5ef0-9b2b-caa1f7fff0d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265691}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4a4af99-78a6-5a4f-84a7-fcfc1b7fb20f" :question/math-academy-id "q-121264" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=15$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ rounded to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(15)=86.185\\,925{…}^{∘}≈{86.19}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${86.19}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={86.19}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{86.19}^{∘}={266.19}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx={86}^{∘},{266}^{∘}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a94023f5-c2de-53f3-99d1-0122ee6a1352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\,600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265699} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f414ec-c23e-5c94-a1ef-cc5ac0d12b70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\,300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265700} {:answer/id #uuid "bef1c2d1-4e66-59d1-bdaf-9f5f726d2934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\,300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265701} {:answer/id #uuid "81efa90b-43dc-5032-80c8-9e3077034f82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265702} {:answer/id #uuid "994c292f-1380-58e3-bc58-04f84532ce4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "994c292f-1380-58e3-bc58-04f84532ce4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265703} :answer-field/id #uuid "39335906-7965-5b7b-b39c-0f411fbdcdcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265698}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09744146-6a55-5a6c-9779-7507baea6402" :question/math-academy-id "q-121332" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1=4$  for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1 & =4 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})={30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${30}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={30}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-{180}^{∘}+{x}_{1}=-{180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}=-{150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-{150}^{∘},{30}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-150\\cdot 30=-4\\,500.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce68ef0f-3cb2-5124-85b3-d207736d1ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265706} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ab487f-304a-5b85-8e84-4a65202a28aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265707} {:answer/id #uuid "f5fa732c-faac-5309-917d-db998fef904d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265708} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4b1db6-69f0-5280-b7f3-38aa8d055c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265709} {:answer/id #uuid "d369c9f5-9662-5cd1-868d-408562a68b4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5fa732c-faac-5309-917d-db998fef904d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265708} :answer-field/id #uuid "843d392a-3e80-5b0d-b9e3-6e9c678a8807" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265705}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "57cf5fd6-82f4-5843-a107-b49508195a40" :question/math-academy-id "q-121545" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/0d956ac6b75c38bfbc5650966880a4eedaf69a0659407fb137d88d30fea08ab7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\sqrt{3}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $A.$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<0.$ Hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $B.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $-\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1157eb80-1f9e-5b70-bdde-7143e7f7697a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265713} {:answer/id #uuid "05a65956-3758-57b0-941c-0b7deac4b381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265714} {:answer/id #uuid "c89c7f20-18a9-5905-8ec7-707cd71c6651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265715} {:answer/id #uuid "5168d962-6b6d-597e-a9d7-70a2f777dfd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265716} {:answer/id #uuid "9caa6984-0aa0-5ce7-a4f5-c760d003359a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1157eb80-1f9e-5b70-bdde-7143e7f7697a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265713} :answer-field/id #uuid "5366fc1f-4ae5-5a1a-bf03-f118b1c17f0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265712}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f77a0be-54c9-59a4-987f-02f55232c640" :question/math-academy-id "q-20482" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/95be2e7bf1dc425e0f0dd9ba818a6a06d0c9afc7874213194f68b1dd426cb110.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=1.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $0\\le x\\le 2\\pi $ hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $A.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "794bfa79-e9e8-5f66-9d8e-11d8fc80c855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "794bfa79-e9e8-5f66-9d8e-11d8fc80c855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265720} :answer-field/id #uuid "76891085-9a1e-5780-b53b-3bf9e217dc83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ade23cd1-e194-580f-85b9-ec3705132ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ade23cd1-e194-580f-85b9-ec3705132ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265722} :answer-field/id #uuid "9575f516-0acc-5c18-9b79-a4f955c7a0c5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265721}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e4a363d-d38a-53ed-83e1-c9aea0002379" :question/math-academy-id "q-274508" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})={30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${30}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={30}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{x}_{1} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={210}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=30\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=210\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "424803f4-87be-5f34-ab1e-acf42aecc55a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "424803f4-87be-5f34-ab1e-acf42aecc55a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265725} :answer-field/id #uuid "8590ccc9-cfcb-5318-997e-3f893c961346" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f62e37e4-70f2-5f79-9cd1-409293dce939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f62e37e4-70f2-5f79-9cd1-409293dce939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265727} :answer-field/id #uuid "16205a8b-891b-52be-88a1-9081088162f6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265726}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ce4a7c1-f895-54e6-aeab-6c701b4779c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-274523" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-{30}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{30}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{x}_{1}={180}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}={150}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-30\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=150\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b915c3fc-977c-5d0b-a46d-bc5462d4b2a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265730} {:answer/id #uuid "eed7bdd9-bb61-57fd-b6de-f955cfa8bc05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eed7bdd9-bb61-57fd-b6de-f955cfa8bc05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265731} :answer-field/id #uuid "235d7247-3fae-5bee-9fb4-fa464187a226" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2530d4ff-120d-58d4-a9d2-8b1ebfb2d585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2530d4ff-120d-58d4-a9d2-8b1ebfb2d585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265733} :answer-field/id #uuid "91136653-2103-5f86-afeb-9e183499d2f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265732}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57779c0f-dbe5-516f-bc87-10d3b3bb9965" :question/math-academy-id "q-321292" :question/problem "Find the **exact solutions in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies outside the given domain its not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=2\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "988e2290-bcd6-52be-b3a6-9e2ba1dcf375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "988e2290-bcd6-52be-b3a6-9e2ba1dcf375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265736} :answer-field/id #uuid "a148d82a-6f80-5c65-a38c-751445abda9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6017ea7-438d-5b90-b1bd-4b0fe2f4f049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6017ea7-438d-5b90-b1bd-4b0fe2f4f049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265738} :answer-field/id #uuid "748ffd06-1180-5721-8833-6dad91ea3e3c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265737}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e6bb08d-3b84-539c-a7fd-00e965243df2" :question/math-academy-id "q-321345" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\sqrt{3}=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\sqrt{3})={60}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${60}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={60}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{x}_{1} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ={240}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=60\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=240\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f388646-b956-518f-83df-6a49a642bd64" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a36dcdf3-791d-57f1-a976-493e0f834822" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a36dcdf3-791d-57f1-a976-493e0f834822" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265741} :answer-field/id #uuid "da7ba1a8-3e0f-54b6-bc49-d0ca7d4edcc9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011b1516-acab-5c2c-9060-faec17381111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "330" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "011b1516-acab-5c2c-9060-faec17381111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "330" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265743} :answer-field/id #uuid "86485b49-6eed-5a6e-a6c3-8a4ece4b51d1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265742}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b702e76f-8945-5678-825a-81c99d35b854" :question/math-academy-id "q-321347" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ is outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={180}^{∘}+(-{30}^{∘})={150}^{∘}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}+(-{30}^{∘})={330}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=150\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=330\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c1db736-47c4-5884-97a2-64793a6995ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c1db736-47c4-5884-97a2-64793a6995ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265746} :answer-field/id #uuid "226182eb-75df-5f62-91f7-8a1158dfca83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aad80ec1-0d8b-50cb-9761-67066f15300b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aad80ec1-0d8b-50cb-9761-67066f15300b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265748} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4862876-3eb2-5bbb-96b9-76d718bc7d03" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265747}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06864fae-c36a-53a1-a62e-b25077497fb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-321633" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-7=0.5$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-7 & =0.5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =7.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7.5)=1.438\\,244…≈1.4\n$$\n\nSince $1.4$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.4.$\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +1.438\\,244…≈4.6.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=1.4$ and $x=4.6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a523010-30af-5dfb-866d-3823347f57c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a523010-30af-5dfb-866d-3823347f57c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265751} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d59f953-f214-5f32-be00-d46351abe97f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265750} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0219bf-f213-539e-bea3-96788d5ca7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c0219bf-f213-539e-bea3-96788d5ca7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265753} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4072c17-cf94-5797-b3ff-b701ab8e898d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265752}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d722d701-1483-5b11-9d46-d8313fd03803" :question/math-academy-id "q-321725" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-3=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-3 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})=0.643\\,501…≈0.6\n$$\n\nSince $0.6$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.6.$\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +0.643\\,501…≈3.8.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=0.6$ and $x=3.8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3ed868-ac15-5829-9f62-445e5fab8750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265756} {:answer/id #uuid "110fc367-7dda-5b28-ab9b-352ae0a2466f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "110fc367-7dda-5b28-ab9b-352ae0a2466f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265757} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd7d8fc6-7441-50c9-aeb2-5523e2310f8e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265755} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022972ae-9bf9-567a-b3d4-a9ba985a7e82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "022972ae-9bf9-567a-b3d4-a9ba985a7e82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265759} :answer-field/id #uuid "69a9f44f-1bfa-5831-8c74-2b3d1ecb8c07" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265758}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d543f07-f315-5493-a1f8-89213f5f2dee" :question/math-academy-id "q-321831" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2=0.5$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2 & =0.5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1.5)=-0.982\\,794…≈-1.0\n$$\n\nSince $-1.0$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\pi +(-0.982\\,794…)≈2.2,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=2\\pi +(-0.982\\,794…)≈5.3.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=2.2$ and $x=5.3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bb9ad3d-2c6c-534a-bbf8-8737929fde6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265762} {:answer/id #uuid "d3754d64-d59b-5c6c-a6de-c6657aeea82d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3754d64-d59b-5c6c-a6de-c6657aeea82d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265763} :answer-field/id #uuid "31b632ab-5141-545a-a657-232bbe0f540a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b4ce3c5-ffed-5092-a7fa-cf751d3f4dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b4ce3c5-ffed-5092-a7fa-cf751d3f4dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265765} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa1a1e47-0fad-52ec-9936-8ef201c5f389" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265764}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51a0110b-2df6-56e3-9d5a-094cffde5bcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-321879" :question/problem "Find the **exact solutions in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed9c1b5b-e708-51e7-9461-fa69d1b1c641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed9c1b5b-e708-51e7-9461-fa69d1b1c641" 