{:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265773} {:answer/id #uuid "2fcc9d8a-9d25-5f0d-81c7-3b5d148bd28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fcc9d8a-9d25-5f0d-81c7-3b5d148bd28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265774} :answer-field/id #uuid "7625f163-4507-568d-ac7b-3f567a86f4b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b301e7ba-1d40-5def-8eb8-0f549dd58ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b301e7ba-1d40-5def-8eb8-0f549dd58ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265776} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab955803-2746-5eef-a691-38a6d6318efe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265775}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d15bb307-cc1d-5861-9298-e5a7bd9d8b8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-321896" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-0.5)=-0.463\\,647…≈-0.5\n$$\n\nSince $-0.5$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.5$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +(-0.463\\,647…)=2.677\\,945…≈2.7.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=-0.5$ and $x=2.7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8514006d-99ea-5161-9f37-eb9f13dbd801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265779} {:answer/id #uuid "82c42992-a302-59ce-8ec3-ea9527c718f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82c42992-a302-59ce-8ec3-ea9527c718f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265780} :answer-field/id #uuid "355a0cc2-1961-59cb-a988-f660dbf176cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265778}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3caba22-9915-504e-bd4c-02a454ebfe13" :question/math-academy-id "q-322566" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/024a7e545d37295878d7f32efd393310dcf1c2c9f88f124ffc5fe46b05155e2c.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$\n\nThe **exact** value of the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ is \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $-\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =x+(-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89bfcde6-510f-520f-a35f-be09e4e13a54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265783} {:answer/id #uuid "723224dc-4baa-565e-b25a-1eafdd8e5a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "723224dc-4baa-565e-b25a-1eafdd8e5a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265784} :answer-field/id #uuid "89517520-5831-5f1e-9edb-49bc2f2a025d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265782}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa7635fe-efad-5976-a9f0-503e368f4d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-322701" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/e03611d72e1c88d1e49806ede117b6808186de27346e426104dca69391f29bbf.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$\n\nThe **exact** value of the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ is \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{5\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $2\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x+2\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0a37c0f-dd67-5ca8-a25c-eb93b7052348" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265787} {:answer/id #uuid "9498ee2b-ce67-58c9-9cbe-f759ded3bdfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265788} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd3bb58-7191-5f73-9993-8e8cf4a568c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265789} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2b7ab4-04d9-53cb-abcb-cfda1bfd8d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265790} {:answer/id #uuid "95a57a8c-8830-5465-b7d7-0692771a6ced" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9498ee2b-ce67-58c9-9cbe-f759ded3bdfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265788} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c9e7ca5-65f2-5ed1-821f-2d5ac50c26e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265786}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f824808a-65d2-53a3-8fad-f1c4f0373d54" :question/math-academy-id "q-72831" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952589/assets/23b4f6296c9e840ad90b8235fa66f17e767c61a6cfeac5bc9566fd1fbd35b004.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$ Find, in radians, the $x$-coordinate of the point $A.$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\n Now, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ ."}]}
